{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you enter.</b> After inheritance and settlement, as it is written: ״כרמך, שדך״ — when each person recognizes what is his." "<b>And the land shall rest.</b> An expression of cessation. One might think: from digging pits, ditches, and caves? Scripture says: ״שדך לא תזרע, וכרמך לא תזמור״ — your field you shall not sow, and your vineyard you shall not prune." "<b>A sabbath to YHWH.</b> A sign that the land belongs to me — that it rests for my Name." "<b>A sabbath to YHWH.</b> Rashi: for the name of HaShem — that is, your intent should not be to leave it fallow in order to improve it, but rather in order to fulfill the commandment of the Holy One, blessed be He."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:05.066235582Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}